        "category": "correctness",
        "consequence": "The `queued` value on every assignment source is the process start time, not when the assignment was queued. Anything that reads `queued` to order or expire sources, or to debug them, gets wrong data. The value is also serialized into the Celery task payload by `to_dict`.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "source:new:src/sentry/integrations/services/assignment_source.py@sha256:885ab5f3b8ef5398cf84e90112d9352978908c663d9034ef89e7ed4eccfdfa0e"
        ],
        "explanation": "`queued: datetime = timezone.now()` calls `timezone.now()` once, when the class body runs at module import. Every `AssignmentSource` built without an explicit `queued`, including all those from `from_integration`, gets that same stale import-time timestamp. A `default_factory` (`field(default_factory=timezone.now)`, which also needs `field` imported from dataclasses) would give each instance its own time.",
